<h2 id="aciubtdd-delegate-aciub" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. Classic delegate — aciub (required)</h2>

**Read and execute** continuous-loop behavior from:

**`.cursor/rules/aciub-allow-continue-iterations-until-blocked.mdc`** (**`aciub`**)

That covers: no-handoff, no permission spam between phases, exwar gate per phase, progress protocol, env-sync (SQLite + Postgres bootstrap), loop-closure / Active Next Step, master-plan sidetracks, and stop conditions.

**Non-TDD loop behavior lives in the classic aciub file.** Edit classic **`aciub`** once when shared loop rules change.

**Override:** [loop order](#aciubtdd-loop) replaces classic **`code → test → fix`** with **`test → code → test → fix`** (or smoke-after-delete path per **implreftdd**).

When classic **aciub** says “follow **implref**”, under **`aciubtdd`** follow **implreftdd** instead.

