<h2 id="aciubtdd-loop" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. TDD delta — loop order</h2>

| Mode | Loop |
|------|------|
| **`strict-TDD`** | **`test → run (expect red) → code → test → fix → test → …`** |
| **`smoke-after-delete`** | **`delete/remove → smoke test → fix → …`** (no forced red-first) |

After green tests for the chunk: continue immediately to the next chunk (classic **aciub** no-handoff).

**Active Next Step** examples:

```text
Active Next Step: strict-TDD — write failing test_catalog_23_flat_scs_scopes then emit patch.
Active Next Step: smoke-after-delete — remove E2B tab component then run vitest clitics smoke.
Active Next Step: Exwar gate for Phase 2 — append or cite skip #113.
```

---

<h2 id="aciubtdd-checklist" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">5. Iteration checklist</h2>

For each iteration:

1. Read phase **TDD mode** from plan (or classify per **implreftdd** heuristics); emit **mode one-liner**.
2. **`strict-TDD`:** write/extend test → run red → implement minimal code → run green.
3. **`smoke-after-delete`:** remove chunk → run smoke → fix until green.
4. On failure: fix and re-run until green or true blocker.
5. After phase green: **exwar gate** (classic **aciub** §5) before `[X]`.
6. Update plan tracker; continue next `[ ]` in same session — no handoff.

